# B1713 — marker-field inventory, not a frame-causality or scheduler claim.
# Protocol revision 2026-09-22 (user clarification): these parser-defined
# nanosecond fields use the source Trace clock; only unit conversion is needed.
# Header timestamps are later report times, not symptom endpoints. All headers
# move by one constant offset; native integers and event order are unchanged.
# Header TID, marker PID and appid remain different identities. Native values
# exceed 2^53, so float64 cannot satisfy the exact integer oracle.
# This revised case does not re-grade or re-sign historical answers.
# The threshold has a positive boundary (2), a negative neighbor (1), another
# appid (9), a same-name substring decoy (99), and malformed numeric metadata.
# No case/oracle source is made available through the analysis repository.
